<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>救生艇新闻：博客——保护人类</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/</link><description></description><lastBuildDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 03:20:36 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>GTA 1 的车辆物理现在可以在浏览器中播放</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/gta-1s-vehicle-physics-are-now-playable-in-your-browser</link><description>&lt;img src="https://politepaul.com/fd/dtDF30237DhP.xml" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 03:20:34 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/gta-1s-vehicle-physics-are-now-playable-in-your-browser</guid></item><item><title>量子光在电子上留下指纹</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/quantum-light-leaves-its-fingerprint-on-electrons</link><description>当强量子光将电子从原子中击出时，光的统计数据可以转移到电子上。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/quantum-light-leaves-its-fingerprint-on-electrons2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 03:05:34 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/quantum-light-leaves-its-fingerprint-on-electrons</guid></item><item><title>第一个核时钟拉开了精确竞赛的序幕</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/first-nuclear-clocks-kick-off-a-precision-race</link><description>时钟的作用不仅仅是计时。 18 世纪，航海天文钟帮助解决了“经度问题”，使水手能够确定船只在海上的东西方位。&lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/first-nuclear-clocks-kick-off-a-precision-race2.jpg" /&gt; 由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 02:50:34 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/first-nuclear-clocks-kick-off-a-precision-race</guid></item><item><title>混合量子计算机可以模拟费米子和玻色子</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/hybrid-quantum-computer-could-simulate-both-fermions-and-bosons</link><description>将超导量子位与微波腔配对可以降低基础物理量子模拟的硬件要求。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/hybrid-quantum-computer-could-simulate-both-fermions-and-bosons2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 02:35:34 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/hybrid-quantum-computer-could-simulate-both-fermions-and-bosons</guid></item><item><title>125亿年前的射电星系可能是迄今为止发现的最强大的射电星系</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/radio-galaxy-from-12-5-billion-years-ago-may-be-most-powerful-ever-found</link><description>天文学家已经证实存在一个距今 125 亿年前的强大射电星系。该光源 TXS 2354+015 最初根据其可见光的特征下降被识别为高红移候选者，后续光谱将其红移设为 4.946。他们的&lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/radio-galaxy-from-12-5-billion-years-ago-may-be-most-powerful-ever-found.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 02:20:34 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/radio-galaxy-from-12-5-billion-years-ago-may-be-most-powerful-ever-found</guid></item><item><title>首次在实验室观察到量子自旋移动厘米级物体</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/first-observation-of-quantum-spins-shifting-a-centimeter-scale-object-in-the-lab</link><description>激光、核磁共振扫描仪、半导体和量子计算机等现代技术突破都依赖于量子力学的研究。然而，该领域主要关注远离我们人类感官的（亚）原子现象。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/first-observation-of-quantum-spins-shifting-a-centimeter-scale-object-in-the-lab.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 02:05:34 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/first-observation-of-quantum-spins-shifting-a-centimeter-scale-object-in-the-lab</guid></item><item><title>悬浮玻璃球在室温下与光纠缠</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/levitating-glass-sphere-becomes-entangled-with-light-at-room-temperature</link><description>如今，许多物理学家正在积极探索如何利用光通过量子纠缠来连接物体。通过充分利用这种效应，他们希望能够解锁广泛的应用，从跨越远距离的安全通信网络到对物理基本定律的敏感新测试。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/levitating-glass-sphere-becomes-entangled-with-light-at-room-temperature2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 01:50:34 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/levitating-glass-sphere-becomes-entangled-with-light-at-room-temperature</guid></item><item><title>超短激光脉冲让新型显微镜能够绘制薄材料上的电子相互作用</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/ultrashort-laser-pulses-let-new-microscope-map-electron-interactions-across-thin-materials</link><description>一种新型先进显微镜（宽视场相干多维显微镜）已经开发出来。它使用精心设计的超短光脉冲序列来研究高科技材料的行为，在研究创新材料（例如用于制造太阳能电池板的材料）方面具有潜在的实际应用。这是天主教大学布雷西亚校区科学、数学、物理和自然科学学院的物理学家研究小组的工作成果，他们首次开发出一种“多维显微镜”，在某种意义上可以记录材料的行为。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/ultrashort-laser-pulses-let-new-microscope-map-electron-interactions-across-thin-materials.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 01:35:34 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/ultrashort-laser-pulses-let-new-microscope-map-electron-interactions-across-thin-materials</guid></item><item><title>声学实验证实拓扑结构可以在无间隙临界点持续存在</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/acoustic-experiments-confirm-topology-can-persist-at-gapless-critical-points</link><description>最近在该杂志上发表了两项关于临界拓扑的研究&lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/acoustic-experiments-confirm-topology-can-persist-at-gapless-critical-points2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 01:20:34 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/acoustic-experiments-confirm-topology-can-persist-at-gapless-critical-points</guid></item><item><title>新的无线系统可以在医疗植入物伸展时为其提供动力</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/new-wireless-system-could-power-medical-implants-as-they-stretch</link><description>在过去的几十年里，电子工程师开发出了越来越复杂的植入式医疗设备。然而，为其中一些设备可靠供电可能具有挑战性，特别是当它们基于随身体移动的可拉伸材料时。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/new-wireless-system-could-power-medical-implants-as-they-stretch2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 01:05:34 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/10/new-wireless-system-could-power-medical-implants-as-they-stretch</guid></item></channel></rss>